WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:03.500
Speaker 1: One more January six story that
I want to go over.

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:11.480
It is now being reported that Republican Senator
Lindsey Graham allegedly told police on January

00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:14.809
6th about the rioters.

00:00:14.809 --> 00:00:18.450
You've got guns, use them, you've got guns.

00:00:18.450 --> 00:00:19.860
Use them now.

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:21.800
Why would we care about this?

00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:24.700
There's actually two reasons which I will
tell you in a moment.

00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:29.100
Let's first look at a report about this that
aired on CNN.

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:33.390
Speaker 2: Graham, according to your report,
yelled at the Senate sergeant at arms.

00:00:33.390 --> 00:00:34.390
What are you doing?

00:00:34.390 --> 00:00:35.390
Take back the Senate.

00:00:35.390 --> 00:00:36.829
You've got guns.

00:00:36.829 --> 00:00:37.829
Use them.

00:00:37.829 --> 00:00:41.710
The South Carolina senator was adamant we
give you guns for a reason.

00:00:41.710 --> 00:00:44.309
He repeated, Use them.

00:00:44.309 --> 00:00:48.590
Another stark contrast to show how the Republican
Party, you know, they've been whitewashing

00:00:48.590 --> 00:00:51.440
Jan. six ever since that day.

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:56.719
But at that time, somebody like Lindsey Graham
was obviously very afraid of what was going

00:00:56.719 --> 00:01:01.850
on and was calling on law enforcement there
to resort to some very extreme measures.

00:01:01.850 --> 00:01:07.110
Speaker 1: So there's a few really important
and interesting things here.

00:01:07.110 --> 00:01:14.810
First of all, a lot of these Republicans who
in retrospect claim January six wasn't that

00:01:14.810 --> 00:01:16.430
bad.

00:01:16.430 --> 00:01:19.490
We weren't really that much at risk, et cetera.

00:01:19.490 --> 00:01:22.650
Leaking, leaking, leaking, drip, drip, drip.

00:01:22.650 --> 00:01:26.620
We're figuring out their actions and their
words.

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:30.400
Both spoke to the degree of insanity that
took place on that day.

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:37.270
Give you an example, Congressman Mo Brooks,
we found out, wore body armor that day.

00:01:37.270 --> 00:01:41.580
Why do you wear body armor unless you expect
things to get really crazy now?

00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:46.210
Mo Brooks has since said, My wife wanted me
to wear it.

00:01:46.210 --> 00:01:48.430
But why did your wife think that there was
going to be fine?

00:01:48.430 --> 00:01:55.430
I mean, it's not really an explanation that
takes Mo Brooks out of knowing in advance

00:01:55.430 --> 00:01:59.350
that there was a real potential for violence,
as one example.

00:01:59.350 --> 00:02:02.340
Now we have Lindsey Graham, Lindsey Graham,
who has downplayed everything.

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:03.340
Is it?

00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:07.560
Listen, some people acted inappropriately,
but most of what happened was constitutionally

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:10.959
protected speech and speech alone, et cetera,
et cetera.

00:02:10.959 --> 00:02:15.629
He was afraid enough that he was telling police
officers to start shooting protesters.

00:02:15.629 --> 00:02:20.239
And the story that they tell in retrospect
clearly doesn't match up with their actions

00:02:20.239 --> 00:02:25.439
on that day, nor does it match up with the
words that are now being ascribed to them.

00:02:25.439 --> 00:02:29.959
There's a good Newsweek article about this,
which says Senator Lindsey Graham reportedly

00:02:29.959 --> 00:02:34.349
called for rioters to be shot as lawmakers
were forced to evacuate the Senate chamber

00:02:34.349 --> 00:02:35.959
on January 6th.

00:02:35.959 --> 00:02:39.769
The Washington Post Sunday published the results
of a lengthy investigation reconstructing

00:02:39.769 --> 00:02:41.989
what happened before, during and after the
riot.

00:02:41.989 --> 00:02:46.450
The second part, titled Bloodshed, goes into
detail about how then Vice President Mike

00:02:46.450 --> 00:02:51.590
Pence and members of Congress were evacuated,
as we know, according to the Post.

00:02:51.590 --> 00:02:56.489
Graham, a Republican from South Carolina,
was furious that senators were forced to flee

00:02:56.489 --> 00:02:57.560
their own chamber.

00:02:57.560 --> 00:03:03.209
He yelled that the sergeant at arms and earned
urged him to shoot rioters in the mob.

00:03:03.209 --> 00:03:06.909
The newspaper reported, citing a Republican
senator with knowledge of the exchange.

00:03:06.909 --> 00:03:07.909
What are you doing?

00:03:07.909 --> 00:03:08.909
Take back the Senate.

00:03:08.909 --> 00:03:09.909
You've got guns.

00:03:09.909 --> 00:03:10.909
Use them.

00:03:10.909 --> 00:03:11.909
We give you guns for a reason.

00:03:11.909 --> 00:03:12.909
Use them.

00:03:12.909 --> 00:03:16.310
Immediately after the riot, Graham turned
against Donald Trump and refused to join his

00:03:16.310 --> 00:03:20.380
GOP colleagues in objecting to the certification
of Biden's win.

00:03:20.380 --> 00:03:22.500
Trump and I, we've had a hell of a journey.

00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:24.129
I hate to end it this way.

00:03:24.129 --> 00:03:25.810
Oh my God, I hate it.

00:03:25.810 --> 00:03:29.999
From my point of view, he's been a consequential
president, but today all I can say is count

00:03:29.999 --> 00:03:30.999
me out.

00:03:30.999 --> 00:03:32.329
Enough is enough.

00:03:32.329 --> 00:03:37.959
But he soon fell back in line defending Trump
as he was impeached a historic second time

00:03:37.959 --> 00:03:40.730
over the Capitol insurrection earlier this
year.

00:03:40.730 --> 00:03:45.200
Graham insisted Trump remains the most popular
Republican in the country and is essential

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:47.209
to the GOP going forward.

00:03:47.209 --> 00:03:51.629
To try to erase Donald Trump from the Republican
Party is insane, and the people who try to

00:03:51.629 --> 00:03:54.739
erase him are going to wind up getting erased.

00:03:54.739 --> 00:03:59.370
It's impossible for this party to move forward
without President Trump being its leader because

00:03:59.370 --> 00:04:03.629
the people who are conservatives have chosen
him as their leader.

00:04:03.629 --> 00:04:08.200
So when we think about what happened on January
six and as we learn more about it and we learn

00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:13.739
about who knew what, when and what were people
expecting at different points in time, remember

00:04:13.739 --> 00:04:19.620
that their actions and their words on that
day tell us much more than their words today.

00:04:19.620 --> 00:04:21.199
It was no big deal.

00:04:21.199 --> 00:04:22.800
These were mostly peaceful protests.

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:23.800
Etc..

00:04:23.800 --> 00:04:26.240
Lindsey Graham saying shoot the protesters.

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:31.729
Mo Brooks wearing body armor, et cetera, et
cetera, they've been lying all along in the

00:04:31.729 --> 00:04:34.110
aftermath of January six.

00:04:34.110 --> 00:04:39.581
That belief that understanding just as reinforced
more and more with every passing day, we're

00:04:39.581 --> 00:04:40.650
going to take a quick break.

00:04:40.650 --> 00:04:42.690
I have so much more to cover today.

00:04:42.690 --> 00:04:47.000
For more on all of today's stories, make sure
you're following us on Instagram at David

00:04:47.000 --> 00:05:52.860
Pakman show and you can follow me on Instagram
at David Pakman.

